    {
      "id": "q",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Real or cosmetic deleveraging?\n*Did China's Three Red Lines policy reduce property developers' economic leverage, or did it primarily shift liabilities off the consolidated balance sheet?*  →  [[[number withheld] Home]]",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "width": 2290,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "rq",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### [[Research Question]]\nTopic approved [number withheld] · question final by [number withheld]",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 90,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "pol",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[[Three Red Lines Policy]]**\nliabilities/assets > [number withheld] % · net gearing > [number withheld] % · cash/short-term debt < [number withheld]\n⚠ caps [number withheld]/[number withheld]/[number withheld] % unverified",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 142,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "dh",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### [[Data Overview]]",
      "x": 500,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 60,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "tT001",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "[[T001 A-Share Audit]]\n✅ delivered",
      "x": 1980,
      "y": 30,
      "width": 290,
      "height": 110,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "tT004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "[[T004 Firm Panel and Red-Line Metrics]]\n✅ delivered [number withheld]",
      "x": 1980,
      "y": 670,
      "width": 290,
      "height": 110,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "des",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[[Empirical Design]]**\n① bunching just below the thresholds\n② dose-response DiD, dose = lines breached on [number withheld]\n③ reported vs adjusted leverage",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 284,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 130
    },
    {
      "id": "var",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**[[Variables and Metrics]]**\nrl1–rl3, perpetual gap, minority share, JV share — decided [number withheld]",
      "x": 20,
